                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ceiling and floor agree at integers and differ by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " otherwise.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For any integer $n$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(n)&=\\lceil n\\rceil-\\lfloor n\\rfloor\\\\f(n)&=n-n\\\\f(n)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $n<x<n+1$, the ceiling is $n+1$ and the floor is $n$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\lceil x\\rceil-\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\\\f(x)&=(n+1)-n\\\\f(x)&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nDraw $y=1$ between consecutive integers. For every integer $n$, place an open circle at $(n,1)$ and a filled point at $(n,0)$. This pattern continues in both directions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
