              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 72,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 26,
                "sourceRegion": "Answer book, printed page 604, left column, question 46(a).",
                "description": "Horizontal blue graph at height 1 with open circles above the integers −2, −1, 0, 1 and 2; corresponding filled blue points on the horizontal axis. Black axes have x and y labels, the level 1 is labelled, and representative nonzero integer labels appear beneath the horizontal axis. Horizontal graph arrows indicate continuation. There is no grid or origin label.",
                "mathematics": "For every integer n, f(n)=0. On every open interval (n,n+1), f(x)=1. The displayed window contains the integers −2 through 2; the same holes and isolated points repeat for all integers.",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only. The student question supplies no graph or drawing canvas."
